sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-memory-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-08--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-08--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-memory-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.555"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Cell size, cell number, and tubule diameter were measured across ploidy series and can still be compiled from those papers, which covers the anatomical half of the claim for newts. The further statement that the tissue switches from cell-cell communication to cytoskeletal bending is a mechanism read off the histology, without a molecular dataset that would distinguish those subroutines. The anatomical part is partly checkable; the mechanism switch is not." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In polyploid newt kidneys, measure tubule diameter against ploidy, cell size, and cells per cross-section, and record whether the largest cells form a tubule by bending around themselves. Conserved diameter with falling cell number would support the anatomical claim; diameter scaling with cell size would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The measurements are mid-twentieth-century histology tables, not a modern repository.", "Cytoskeletal bending versus cell-cell signalling is inferred from cell geometry, not from molecular markers.", "The record is limited to salamander kidney tubules." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-08--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2024-memory-08 by Grok 4.7: 0.8" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
